Problem:
 Fetching data is required tp update the states
 Data inconsistency because of dependencies or multiple sources of truth(e.g multiple services)
 Complex data flow which is hard to understand, track and debug
-> solution is to use Global State fr reusing data
NgRx:
    Building reactive appns with a single state
    reactive -> respond to changes

-> checkout NgRxLifecycle.png
STORE:
    Hold the application State(immutable- cannot get changed directly)
ACTIONS:
    Events that modify  the state in the STORE
REDUCERS:
    Functions that take actions and modify the state base on the action type
EFFECTS:
    Handle asynchronous operations(like fetching data from a server) and then trigger new actions

One-way data flow:
Actions ➔ Reducers ➔ Updated State -> Selectors share updates
The updated state is automatically passed to the components via selectors(components subscribe to the selector)

node packages:
    "npm install @ngrx/store @ngrx/effects"

CREATING STATE:
    think about the entity
    - created globally
    "ng g i app.state"  //creates interface AppState
    - its immutable
    - we use Reducers/actions to modify state
    - In this project: we want to store imfo of book in our AppState
        readonly book: Book[]
    - State shd be registered inside a store

CREATING ACTIONS:
    - create books/book.actions.ts under app
    "import { createAction,props } from '@ngrx/store';"
                            props for properties of the book
    export const AddBook = createAction('[Book] Add Book',props<Book>())
    - we are exporting Addbook action, which requires Book to perform the action
        the first argument is type , and u can name it as u like
    - SUCESS AND FAILURE ACTION:
    export const AddBookSuccess = createAction('[Book] Add Book Successfully',props<Book>())
    export const AddBookFailure = createAction('[Book] Add Book Failure',props<{error:any}>())
    
CREATING REDUCER:
    - processes the actions
    - its called a reducer becoz it reduces the {current state , action} to new state
    - create book/book.reducer.ts
    "import { createReducer, on } from '@ngrx/store';"
    - import the actions is need to process
        import { AddBook,RemoveBook } from "./book.actions";
    - AppState can contain different states like book, User , etc.
    - Reducer is specific to one state i.e BookReducer, User will have its own Reducer
       i.e Reducer takes care of only segmet of the AppState not whole.
    - Reducer always needs a initial state
        export const initalState: ReadonlyArray<Book> = [];
    - Reducer flow:
    Copy current state segmet -> make changes -> return new state
    - we use "on" to register actions for this reducer
    export const BookReducer = createReducer(
            //as said before reducer needs initial state to make changes on and return new state
        initalState,
            //inside createReducer we can use "state", this state is not the global state
            //its is the current segment of the state that this reducer shd take care of
            //we take the current state and what we need to add then..
            // we want to create an array 
            // ...state -> copies all the elements from old state into the array
            // and the new book to add
        on(AddBook,(state, {id,title,author}) => [...state, {id,title,author}]),
            //bookId same as we given in the RemoveBook action props<{bookId:string}>()
            //filter returns new state where the array contains books != bookId
        on(RemoveBook,(state,{bookId}) => state.filter(book => book.id != bookId))
    );

CREATING STORE:
    - its a global store, import in app.module.ts
        "import { StoreModule } from '@ngrx/store';"
    - we need to specify the reducer im the root level
        (app.module.ts)
        //tells store to use BookReducer to manage all state changes to book(we defined this in state)
            StoreModule.forRoot({book: BookReducer})

DISPATCH ACTIONS:
    - we start action disptach from within components
    "ng g c book-list"
    constructor(private store: Store<{books: Book[]}>){}
    addBook(id:string,title:string,author:string){
        //dispatch -> to start an action
        this.store.dispatch(AddBook({id,title,author}))
    }

LOADING BOOKS FROM STORE:
    - we create property of type Observable, so as soon as we add books, remove books using 
        our actions which get processed by reducer which changes the state, we will get notified
        as we subscribed to it.
        booklist component:
            books$ : Observable<Book[]>;
            this.books$ = store.pipe(select('books'))

Using AppState interface for Type safety:
    - we have used book in AppState but used books in component 
    which will break functionality. We can use AppState instead of naming everywhere
    - in booklist component:
        constructor(private store: Store<AppState>){
            this.books$ = store.pipe(select('book'))
        }
    - in app module
        StoreModule.forRoot<AppState>({book: BookReducer}),
    - also remove readonly from reducer initialState
    Readonly is not needed as in the createReducer bloxk we are making sure sure that we are not mofidying the state but 
    using it to create new state
        export const initalState: Book[] = [];

HTML NOTES:
    here #bookId is reference and we are using it to pass value to addBook()
    <input #bookId type="text" placeholder="Book Id">
    <input #bookTitle type="text" placeholder="Book Title">
    <input #bookAuthor type="text" placeholder="Author">
    <button (click)="addBook(bookId.value,bookTitle.value,bookAuthor.value)"></button>

Adjusting reducer for effects:
    - add book shd not modify the state directly, when called effect will call a service to 
        add book which connects with db(api) and send the response if success/failure

creating service:
    "ng g service books/book"
    of -> create Observable

CREATING EFFECTS:
 - create books/books.effects.ts
 //we have created an effect which will specifically run when action of type AddBook ocures
    addBook$ = createEffect(() => this.actions$.pipe(
        ofType(bookActions.AddBook),
        //what to do when this action occures
        //here action is book (props)
        //mergeMap helps us to take observables and transform to single observable
        mergeMap((action) => this.bookService.addBook(action)
            .pipe(
                //pipe to say we have something do after book service returns something
                //bookService addBook will return book observable which we are mapping to AddBookSuccess Action
                map(book => bookActions.AddBookSuccess(book)),
                catchError((error) => of(bookActions.AddBookFailure({error})))
            ))
    ))

REGISTERING THE EFFECT:
(in app module)
 EffectsModule.forRoot([BookEffects])

ANGULAR DEV TOOLS, REDUX CHROME EXTENSION for inspecting the effects,actions
to used that u need to install
"npm install @ngrx/store-devtools"
StoreDevtoolsModule.instrument() in app modules.js
